    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2P1JQ9UqE1vsw1UwgGCi9aM)_\n\nFollows #234/#235/#237.\n\n- `:refs`: each citation key (`@key` or `cite:key`) is an `sp-bib:` link that opens the entry in its `.bib` file with `citar-open-entry`. The plain text is unchanged for sorting.\n- `pub-title`: new option `sp-collec-query-note-link-columns` (default `(\"pub-title\")`); those meta columns are shown as `[[id:ID][text]]`, so following it opens the note in Org. In the vui table such a cell is read-only (like other link cells).\n\nI read \"the `:refs` row\" as the `:refs` column and \"pub-title\" as the `pub-title` meta column; tell me if you meant something else.\n\nTested in Emacs 29.3 batch (21 tests, citar stubbed) and the tangle check; not run in the real vault or in the exc/vui widgets.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi8q9zwVhMybYWXqYXq)_",
